>all_greet_prog 100~
if quest(0,4,$n) == 1
  say I hear you have helped our maintenance workers repair our
  say protective dome.  That is good.  It appears, however, that you
  say are not a citizen of this noble city.  I don't know how you got in,
  say but I'm afraid you'll have to be put to death.
  mpmset $n quest 0 4 2
  mptransfer $n 15668
endif
if quest(0,4,$n) == 3
  say You have proven your worth to me.  You shall now be considered
  say a citizen of my noble city.  I know of some valuable real estate   
  say not too far from here... Small RODENT problem... 
  pat $n
  say It looks like you've got some nasty wounds there.
  say You might want to go see my personal healer.  
  say God be with you.
  mpmset $n quest 0 4 4
endif
~
>speech_prog p rodent~
 if quest(8,1,$n)==0
  say Well, it's these damned graven, 
  say When we managed to tap into the Great Mushroom River 
  say for fresh water, some mutant death gerbils managed to 
  say make their way into our outlying homes.  We have since  
  say cultivated flytraps to take care of unwanted rodent
  say migration from the mainland, but we've been unable 
  say to take care of the population which has established a 
  say foothold here.  They've grown rather large, and my botanist 
  say tells me they've actually adapted to conditions here.
  say He calls them 'graven'."  
  shrug $n
  mpechoat $n Prince Arcus continues...
  say Anyway, you'd be doing everyone a favor if you were to 
  say take out a few of these pests.  As an added incentive,
  say you will be rewarded for every 100 graven you slay.
  mpmset $n quest 8 1 1
else
  if quest(8,1,$n)==1
  say Yes yes... kill the graven...
  endif
endif
~
